Description: Sysible Server — headless engineering platform (all-in-one)
 Turns a Debian base into the Sysible Server: the tools a Linux/DevOps/SRE/platform
 engineer reaches for, installed and ready on first boot, so there is no half-hour
 of apt after every fresh install — the same toolset as Sysible Server but
 headless (no GNOME desktop, no Calamares, no GUI applications).
 .
 Depends carries the must-haves (shell, networking, containers via podman, the
 modern CLI set, Python, Ansible, the Sysible CLI). Recommends carries the heavier
 pieces (Docker CE, Kubernetes, OpenTofu, cloud CLIs, headless libvirt/QEMU, the
 language toolchains) so a lean build can drop them with --no-install-recommends.
 .
 Tools that are not in Debian (Docker CE, kubectl/helm, OpenTofu, cloud CLIs) are
 pulled from their upstream apt repositories, which sysible-release configures — so
 `apt install` Just Works without vendoring their binaries.
